2.1 Line Breaking and Page Breaking
2.1.1 Justified Paragraphs
Books are often typeset with each line having the same length. LATEX inserts the necessary line breaks and spaces between words by optimising the contents of a whole paragraph. If necessary, it also hyphenates words that would not fit comfortably on a line. How the paragraphs are typeset depends on the document class. Normally the first line of a paragraph is indented, and there is no additional space between two paragraphs. Refer to subsection 7.6.4 for more information.
In special cases it might be necessary to order LATEX to break a line.
