2.4 Slash (/)
In order to typeset a slash between two words, one can simply type, for example, read/write, but this makes LATEX treat the two words as one. Hyphenation is disabled by the slash character (see subsection 2.1.2), so there may be ‘overfull’ errors. To overcome this, use \slash. For example, type
