The \NewDocumentCommand checks if a command with the given name is already defined, and raises an error if it is. This means you can freely use it to define your own commands without worrying about breaking internal commands used by LATEX or its packages. But sometimes, redefining existing commands is actually what you want. For example, many packages allow customisation in this way. In this, case you should use \RenewDocumentCommand. It works the same way as the former command, but raises an error if a command with the given name is not already defined.
