\title{〈title〉}, \author{〈author〉} and optionally \date{〈date〉}
before calling \maketitle. In the argument to \author, you can supply several names separated by \and commands. An example of some of the commands mentioned above can be found in Listing 1.2 on page 10. Apart from the sectioning commands explained above, LATEX defines four additional commands for use with the book class. They are useful for dividing your publication. The commands alter chapter headings and page numbering to work as you would expect in a book:


