2.16.3 Long Quotations and Poetry
LATEX provides two additional environments: quotation and verse. The quotation environment is useful for longer quotes running over several paragraphs, because it indents the first line of each paragraph. The verse environment is useful for poems where the line breaks are important. The lines are separated by issuing a \\ at the end of a line, and an empty line after each verse. Note that these environments are not defined by csquotes, so they do not accept the optional attribution argument, and are not context sensitive.
