3.2.1 Math Mode
The commands and environments mentioned in the previous section activate a special math-optimised version of the LATEX language. It is commonly known as math mode. LATEX normally operates in text mode. There are numerous differences between the two modes. For starters, most of the whitespace is ignored in math mode.
